# Commits

- A commit is a single Conventional Commits subject line in English, under 70 characters: `feat(web): add manual holdings entry (PLA-26)`. No body and no trailers (`Co-Authored-By:`, `Claude-Session:`).
- PR titles use the same format with the Linear key; PRs are merged with Squash and merge.
- Destructive migrations: `[DESTRUCTIVE]` at the start of the PR title.
- The PR body starts with `## Intent`.
- Describe the current state and why, not how you got there.
